          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "ks.\n\n**Design** (single pipeline in `BaseLoader`, inherited by all loaders):\n- `BaseLoader.__init__(path_transform=None)` stores `path_transform` and `_aliases` (`src/jinja2/loaders.py:74`)\n- `add_alias` / `remove_alias` manage the alias map (`loaders.py:84`); aliases don't chain, can be overwritten, `remove_alias` is idempotent\n- `_resolve_template` returns `(resolved, lookup)`: alias resolved first, then `path_transform` applied. `lookup` is used for the actual source lookup; `resolved` (post-alias, pre-transform) is what `TemplateNotFound` reports \u2014 satisfying both Task 1's \"original name in errors\" and Task 2's \"target name, not alias\"\n- Every loader's `get_source` (and `PrefixLoader`/`ChoiceLoader`/`ModuleLoader` `load`/`get_loader`, since the environment enters through `load`) runs the lookup through this pipeline; `PrefixLoader`/`ChoiceLoader` apply it at the top level before delegating\n- `_make_uptodate` wraps the uptodate callback when a name was loaded via alias, so a cached `Environment` (default auto-reload) revalidates and correctly raises `TemplateNotFound` after `remove_alias`\n- Transform exceptions propagate uncaught; `None`/omitted transform leaves behavior byte-for-byte identical (existing tests confirm)\n\n**Assumptions noted**: alias resolution happens before `path_transform` (per Task 2's \"aliases resolve before normal loading\"); `ModuleLoader` (not in Task 1's list) got both features too for uniformity, since Task 2 requires all subclasses to use aliasing.",
